er dying but then there's also  another major reveal which is the fact  that Mark's mother Steven's mother is  dead which makes you really wonder who  exactly was he talking to on the phone  this whole time now Steven could have  simply been leaving his mother  voicemails but in some of the episodes  it did seem like she was replying to him  even in the scene after the funeral of  his mother it does appear like Stephen  is talking to somebody Mark sits outside  of a house where people are gathered to  mourn the loss of his mother he says  it's a Shiva which is a Jewish week-long  morning period and Mark is Jewish he  decides not to go in even after he sees  his father and his father tells him to  come in he simply walks away now ashiva  is supposed to be a time where a person  Embraces and discusses their loss but  Mark doesn't want to deal with that  that's actually why he invented Stephen  and brought Stephen to life so instead  of dealing with it Steven comes out and  he has no idea where he is he simply  says oh I did it again and what he  thinks it is is just he's getting up at  night and essentially sleepwalking but  he pulls out the phone and it looks like  he is talking to somebody and it sounds  like there is a tiny back and forth he  even goes at one point in time no I know  I did it again like he is reacting to  something somebody is saying but we know  it's not his mom because his mother is  dead now I actually think that he could  simply be talking to himself and maybe  perhaps he is hearing a voice inside of  his mind because if you take a look at  his phone in this scene it's not  actually calling anybody it looks like  it's just kind of on a home screen and  in a show where we're dealing with  mental illness this probably makes sense  that it's kind of in his head which in  turn makes it even more sad now they  returned to the top of the ship where  unfortunately the scales aren't balanced  yet and towerette says she's sorry but  the underworld is es